Description: pco: clamp integer color outputs and image stores to the format
 Fragment outputs to integer attachments with channels narrower than 32 bit
 are bit-packed in pack_to_format() with nir_bitfield_insert, which keeps the
 low bits. Image stores to such formats write the raw 32-bit value, also for
 formatless stores (no pck format for integer formats). Values that do not
 fit therefore wrap. Vulkan leaves out-of-range values undefined for color
 attachments (interfaces.adoc, Fragment Output Interface), but zink and the
 GL state tracker rely on them saturating: u_blitter and the st_pbo shaders
 only clamp at the sign boundary (u_simple_shaders.c, st_pbo.c) and expect
 the store to clamp to the channel width. GL-CTS packed_pixels shows this as
 wrapped instead of saturated GetTexImage/ReadPixels results.
 .
 Clamp each integer channel to its range before packing, and before formatted
 and formatless integer image stores. For formatless stores the descriptor
 pck_info carries an integer flag, the signedness and the bit width minus one
 of each component. The transfer path already clamps the same way
 (pvr_usc.c, pack_int_value()). 32-bit integer formats are unchanged.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
